<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE RESERVES RISE TO S$115.53 BLN IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE RESERVES RISE TO S$115.53 BLN IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's official reserves rose to Singapore $115.53 billion in June, the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said in its monthly statistical bulletin.  </p>
<p>Official foreign reserves:</p>
<p>(billions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>					    June 97   May 97    June 96</p>
<p>    Total official reserves	 115.53    115.18    101.96</p>
<p>Gold and foreign exchange</p>
<p>    reserves			    114.87    114.52    101.29</p>
<p>    Special drawing rights (million)  253.5     253.5     240.4</p>
<p>    Reserve Position in IMF (million) 409.2     409.2     429.3</p>
<p>Source: Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS)</p>
